{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{artist: Irish hymn, translated by Mary Byrne and Eleanor Hull}
{copyright: Public domain}
# A comment line that must not show

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Vision, O [D]Lord of my heart;
[G]Naught be all [A]else to me, [Bm]save that Thou art.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Be Thou my [G]Wisdom, and [D]Thou my true Word;
[G]I ever with [A]Thee and Thou [Bm]with me, Lord.
{end_of_verse}

